5,1,1,talk,Midori,,Hello everyone. I'm looking forward to working with you all to find the right system. I think we should start by looking at how support was handled during the last winter's outage.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree we need a practical approach. I want to examine the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover to see how we actually handle transitions.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,Let's make this interesting! I'm curious about the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift in the 2018 pay move.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I'll focus on the people. I want to look into administrator retirements and hiring times, as well as the depot supervisors and the last rollout.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,A most prudent start. I shall examine the board minutes on capital and operating requests and the five years of renewal invoices to see where the money actually goes.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, that's a great point about the calendar. I'll also look into the warehouse rule changes after new accounts to see if our plans stay relevant.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,I'll also check the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial. We need to know if new software can actually survive our hardware.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
