25,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
26,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems we have a problem with accountability. During the outage, support was scattered and unowned, and our warehouse rules changed almost immediately after the last project started.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The reality on the ground is harsh. We have no freeze window in winter, and our yard devices are so outdated that a general tool was abandoned for spreadsheets.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"I found that our internal tools are aging in place because we can't find time to test upgrades, and external data lifts left us with errors for a year.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are in a precarious position. We're losing key administrators and can't hire replacements, while depot supervisors simply ignore standard training to keep their own routines.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings suggest a pattern of ""hidden"" costs. Capital requests are trimmed, but operating lines pass easily, and separately licensed add-ons have climbed every single year.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that's worrying. If we pick a modular system, will we just see those costs climb? I'm worried about a lack of clear ownership when things break.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Misaki, if the supervisors ignore training, a complex system will fail. We need something that fits the yard as it is, not as the office imagines it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, exactly. If we keep relying on external teams for data moves, we'll just be repairing their mistakes for years. We need something stable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, stability is hard when the people who know the system are retiring. We can't afford a rollout that requires a massive retraining effort for the crews.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, precisely. A fragmented licensing model is a financial trap. We need a predictable cost structure that doesn't surprise us after the initial contract is signed.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Midori,,It sounds like we all fear the same thing: a gap between the plan and the reality. We need a vendor that provides clear ownership and a stable configuration.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I'll be wary of any ""cloud"" solution that doesn't account for our hardware or our peak-season chaos. It has to be rugged.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"I agree. No more ""aging in place"" or external teams leaving us with a mess. The system must be maintainable and the data migration must be clean.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Misaki,,And it must be simple enough for the depot crews to actually use without needing a permanent trainer on site.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic dictates we avoid modular licenses and complex external dependencies. A bundled, predictable cost and a focused deployment seem most rational.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
