53,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
54,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the candidates, Meridian Systems seems the most balanced. A fixed configuration and a regional service team should provide the ownership and stability we lack.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I prefer Anchor Industrial Software. They are built for transport and have engineers present through rollout, which is the only way to survive our yards and calendar.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward Anchor as well. Having the engineering team on-site avoids the ""external repair"" cycle I'm worried about, and on-prem servers avoid the aging-in-place issue.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Anchor seems safest for the crews. With engineers present during rollout, the depot supervisors are more likely to actually adopt the system.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Meridian's hosted suite is tempting for cost predictability, but Anchor's on-prem model with a dedicated team avoids the recurring ""add-on"" traps of subscription marketplaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, @May, @Misaki, if you all prefer Anchor, I can see the merit. The on-site presence would certainly solve the ownership issue I'm concerned about.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""May"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, exactly. A regional team is fine, but having the engineers here during the peak-season pressure is a different level of security.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, do you think Anchor's cost is more stable than Meridian's? I'd hate to see another subscription that creeps up.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Misaki,,I just want to make sure the people aren't overwhelmed. Anchor's approach seems the most supportive of our stretched staff.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Anchor's model is more traditional. While the initial cost is higher, it avoids the ""marketplace"" volatility of Tessera or the modular chaos of Corvus. It is logically sound.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Midori,,I am convinced. The need for on-site support and a system that understands transport outweighs the convenience of a hosted suite. I'll vote for Anchor.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I'm glad we agree. It's the only choice that respects the reality of the depot floor. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,It's the most robust option. No more external data messes or outdated tools. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"For the sake of our administrators and supervisors, this is the right path. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The evidence of our past failures points directly away from modularity and toward dedicated implementation. I also vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
